---
title: Theming
order: 70
tags: [theme, css]
---

quaydoc ships one default theme: a single stylesheet, a small script and one
sidebar template. Custom themes replace any of these by placing files next
to the documentation root.

## Assets

- `assets/style.css` — everything visual,
- `assets/quaydoc.js` — the mobile navigation toggle.

The default stylesheet defines semantic classes you can rely on: `sidebar`,
`toc-panel`, `admonition-*`, `pre.highlight`, `.tok-keyword` and friends,
and a responsive layout that collapses the sidebar below 860 pixels.

## Templates

The sidebar is rendered from the theme template `nav.html`, a small
variables-in-curlies template:

```
{% for item in nav %}
<a class="nav-link{% if item.url == current %} active{% endif %}"
   href="{{ item.url|escape }}">{{ item.title|escape }}</a>
{% endfor %}
```

The template engine supports `{{ expr }}` interpolation with filters,
`{% if %}`, `{% for %}`, and `{% include %}`. See the template engine tests
for the full contract.

## Custom themes

Point `[build] theme` at a directory; any of `assets/style.css`,
`assets/quaydoc.js` or `templates/nav.html` found there overrides the
defaults. The build copies the merged asset set into the output.
